{"id": "EUVD-2026-97052", "enisaUuid": "03407471-17aa-3f0d-92fa-134ab5e38289", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in the AiragAppController queryById handler that allows low-privileged authenticated users to read any AI application configuration. Attackers can enumerate application ids via the unguarded /airag/app/listDict endpoint and query each id to obtain system prompts, memory prompts, model ids, knowledge base ids, and plugin bindings of other users' applications.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:33:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:36:38", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_airag_app_query_by_id.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-boot-module/jeecg-boot-module-airag/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/airag/app/controller/AiragAppController.java#L196-L203", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-airag-app-querybyid"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108878", "GHSA-mf5r-54hh-g48q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e67f9c13-cfdd-3e8d-8acb-301d4290a723", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4be18047-e471-3a4c-875a-e39b1564d88f", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}